  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 356.35pt, "The utilization of two-dimensional (2D) materials in magnetic tunnel junctions (MTJs) ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 372.67pt, "has shown excellent performance and rich physics. As for 2D antiferromagnets, the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 388.87pt, "magnetic moments in different layers respond asynchronously and can be configured at ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 405.19pt, "various states under different magnetic fields, showing the possibility of efficient ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 421.51pt, "magnetic and electrical tunability. In this report, A-type antiferromagnetic (AFM) ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 437.83pt, "material (Fe")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(125.78pt, 438.31pt, "0.5")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(133.94pt, 437.83pt, "Co")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(146.21pt, 438.31pt, "0.5")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(154.25pt, 437.83pt, ")")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(157.61pt, 438.31pt, "5")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(160.85pt, 437.83pt, "GeTe")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(184.13pt, 438.31pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(187.37pt, 437.83pt, " (FCGT) works as electrodes to realize full van der Waals ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 454.15pt, "magnetic tunnel junctions. Owing to the interfacial effect, the even-layer FCGT, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 470.47pt, "although with zero net magnetization, exhibits spin selectivity in MTJ architecture ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 486.67pt, "contributing to a tunneling magnetoresistance (TMR) reaching about 25% at a low ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 503.02pt, "operating current 1 nA at 100 K and persists near room temperature. Due to the surface ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 519.34pt, "spin-flop (SSF) effect in antiferromagnetic FCGT, the alternation flexibility between the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 535.66pt, "volatile and nonvolatile memory behavior is achieved. The interfacial TMR can be tuned ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 551.98pt, "efficiently in amplitude and even sign under different bias currents and temperatures. ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 568.3pt, "These findings show precise magnetoelectric manipulation in MTJs based on 2D ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 584.5pt, "antiferromagnets and highlight the promise of 2D antiferromagnets for spintronic ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 600.82pt, "devices. ")
]

