  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 295.73pt, "3. Conclusion ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 312.05pt, "In summary, this study demonstrates the surface spin-flop transition driven in van der Waals ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 328.25pt, "antiferromagnetic FCGT MTJ. In the FCGT/WSe₂/FCGT heterostructure, even-layer FCGT ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 344.57pt, "exhibits robust tunable interfacial spin polarization in a wide temperature range. By confining ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 360.91pt, "the magnetic field range up to room temperature, the system allows versatile alternation ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 377.23pt, "between nonvolatile and volatile functionality. The sign and magnitude of the interfacial spin ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 393.55pt, "polarization are highly tunable via bias current. Our work highlights the application of ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 409.87pt, "interfacial spin polarization and surface spin-flop in antiferromagnetic MTJ architectures.  ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 426.07pt, "4. Methods ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 442.39pt, "Sample and device fabrication")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(194.21pt, 442.39pt, ":")
  #line-at(199.61pt, 442.39pt, "The process for fabricating FCGT/WSe")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(358.18pt, 443.35pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(361.42pt, 442.39pt, "/FCGT MTJ devices ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 458.71pt, "began with the acquisition of high-quality van der Waals (vdW) bulk single crystals of FCGT, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 475.03pt, "hBN, and WSe")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(134.9pt, 475.99pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(138.14pt, 475.03pt, " from HQ Graphene. We first exfoliated FCGT flakes onto on SiO")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(418.54pt, 475.99pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(421.78pt, 475.03pt, " (285 ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 491.35pt, "nm)/Si substrates using adhesive tape. The Pt electrodes were fabricated using standard e-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 507.7pt, "beam lithography and ultrahigh vacuum magnetron sputtering techniques. Next, FCGT and ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 523.9pt, "WSe")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(91.344pt, 524.86pt, "2")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(94.584pt, 523.9pt, " flakes, carefully chosen for their thickness and shape, were transferred onto these pre-")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 540.22pt, "patterned electrodes. The 2D heterostructure was accomplished using a dry transfer method")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 6.48pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(435pt, 536.74pt, "51")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(441.48pt, 540.22pt, ". ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 556.54pt, "To protect the FCGT layer from oxidation, the entire heterostructure was encapsulated with a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 572.86pt, "thick layer of hBN. Finally, the device was annealed at 120 °C for 30 minutes to improve the ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 589.18pt, "contact between the different layers and to remove any air bubbles that might have been ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 605.5pt, "trapped during the transfer process. It is noted that all transfer steps were performed inside a ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 621.7pt, "nitrogen-filled glovebox, where the levels of oxygen and water were kept below 0.01 ppm, ")
  #line-at(72.024pt, 638.04pt, "ensuring a clean interface and preventing contamination. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72.024pt, 654.36pt, "Spin valve measurements")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 9.96pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(176.69pt, 654.36pt, ":")
  #line-at(183.77pt, 654.36pt, "Transport properties at low temperatures and as a function of ")
